7. FIREBASE SECURITY AND USER PRIVACY
==================================================

Implement secure multi-user Firebase authorization.

## Firestore Rules

Every user must only be able to access records belonging to their own authenticated UID.

Use the equivalent of:

request.auth != null &&
request.auth.uid == userId

Apply appropriate validation to document creation, updates, and deletion.

## Storage Rules

Store attachments in user-specific paths, such as:

users/{uid}/receipts/{fileName}

Only the authenticated owner can read or write those files.

## Additional Security

- Never expose private financial data publicly.
- Never expose privileged Firebase credentials in the frontend.
- Never rely exclusively on frontend route guards.
- Protect Firebase Storage.
- Reject unauthenticated database access.
- Do not allow user-to-user data access.
- Validate ownership of referenced records.
- Add upload size and file type restrictions.
- Use server-side secrets for Gemini API calls.
- Provide complete Firestore and Storage Security Rules.

Every user must have access only to their own personal finance workspace.

