When the internet returns, sync pending changes automatically.

Important:

- A new device requires an internet connection for its first login.
- Previously cached data may be available offline only on that device.
- Cloud data becomes available on other devices after successful login and synchronization.
- Firestore Web persistence is not supported in every browser, so detect capability and provide a fallback.
- Do not claim offline support when the browser has not enabled it.

### Device Privacy

If a user signs out from a shared device:

- Warn about pending unsynced records.
- Do not lose pending work silently.
- Separate user-specific local data.
- Prevent the next user from viewing the previous user's cached information.
- Clear or securely isolate application-specific local data.
- Do not display private records before the new authentication state is verified.

Ask users whether a device is trusted before retaining sensitive offline financial data.

